WEBVTT

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:02.784
Grid Bot Builder. Grid Bot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.616
Lesson one. Introduction. Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:10.997
Not financial advice. This is general

00:00:10.997 --> 00:00:13.504
information and doesn't consider your

00:00:13.504 --> 00:00:16.164
objectives, financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:19.439
Crypto is high risk. You could lose all

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:22.488
the money you put in. Crypto carries a

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:26.104
risk of total loss. The prices are public

00:00:26.104 --> 00:00:29.193
historical daily closes, marked Example. A

00:00:29.193 --> 00:00:32.627
close is the last price of the day. Past

00:00:32.627 --> 00:00:35.191
performance is not a reliable indicator of

00:00:35.191 --> 00:00:38.973
future results. A grid bot places waiting

00:00:38.973 --> 00:00:41.495
buy orders on lines below the price and

00:00:41.495 --> 00:00:43.939
sell orders on lines above it, inside a

00:00:43.939 --> 00:00:46.672
top and a bottom you choose. The space

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:49.450
between your top and your bottom is called

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.096
the band. A limit order is an order that

00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:54.778
waits at a price you choose. It does not

00:00:54.778 --> 00:00:58.478
chase the price. The sells above need some

00:00:58.478 --> 00:01:00.969
coin, so a grid starts with part cash and

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:03.459
part coin, and that is a description, not

00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:06.337
advice about what to hold. Cash is money

00:01:06.337 --> 00:01:10.284
you can spend. Coin is the crypto. A stop

00:01:10.284 --> 00:01:12.633
is a rule you write down before you start,

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:14.697
saying what you will do if the price

00:01:14.697 --> 00:01:16.904
leaves the band and does not come back.

00:01:18.104 --> 00:01:20.752
When a chart says Example, it means a real

00:01:20.752 --> 00:01:22.999
past price used as an example, not a

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:26.498
forecast. By the end you will know what a

00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:30.675
grid bot places. You will see that idea on

00:01:30.675 --> 00:01:34.690
one real path from 2023. You will be able

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:36.746
to say the stop rule in one sentence.

00:01:37.765 --> 00:01:40.058
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall. The

00:01:40.058 --> 00:01:42.711
rungs wait, and they do not chase you. The

00:01:42.711 --> 00:01:44.906
ladder is the analogy, and the chart

00:01:44.906 --> 00:01:48.415
beside it is the real past path. The range

00:01:48.415 --> 00:01:50.415
is the top line and the bottom line,

00:01:50.394 --> 00:01:53.089
copied from the path. Every close in this

00:01:53.089 --> 00:01:55.622
window stayed between those two lines. A

00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:57.845
neat round box would have sat inside the

00:01:57.823 --> 00:02:00.158
real lines, so it does not match the path.

00:02:01.007 --> 00:02:03.383
The range is a top and a bottom you draw

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:05.908
before any rung. Without a top and a

00:02:05.908 --> 00:02:09.166
bottom, you can't place the lines. Six

00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:11.515
equal gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:02:11.515 --> 00:02:14.187
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:02:14.707 --> 00:02:17.458
Seven lines make those six gaps. A limit

00:02:17.458 --> 00:02:19.952
order waits on a level. It does not run

00:02:19.952 --> 00:02:22.940
after the price. The levels are limit

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:25.409
orders that wait on the rungs. A limit

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:28.188
order sits at a price. It does not chase.

00:02:29.388 --> 00:02:31.716
A fence has a top rail and a bottom rail.

00:02:32.236 --> 00:02:35.058
Inside them, the price can wander. On the

00:02:35.058 --> 00:02:37.441
chart those rails are the bottom line and

00:02:37.441 --> 00:02:40.674
the top line. The daily close is the last

00:02:40.674 --> 00:02:43.479
price of the day. Crypto trades all day,

00:02:43.479 --> 00:02:46.197
so the day is cut at a set time. This

00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:50.381
candle is 19 July 2023. The high, the low,

00:02:50.381 --> 00:02:53.085
and the close are labelled. A wick is the

00:02:53.085 --> 00:02:55.332
thin line from the close out to the high

00:02:55.332 --> 00:02:57.763
or the low. The wick shows price went

00:02:57.763 --> 00:02:59.987
there briefly, then came back before the

00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:03.167
day closed. The example is Bitcoin's

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:06.584
public daily price in US dollars. From 19

00:03:06.584 --> 00:03:10.806
July 2023 to 16 October 2023, every one of

00:03:10.806 --> 00:03:15.165
those days closed inside the band. We do

00:03:15.165 --> 00:03:17.670
not need to read each day. The shape is

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.840
the lesson, and it is marked Example. A

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.118
stop is a rule you write down before you

00:03:23.118 --> 00:03:25.182
start, saying what you will do if the

00:03:25.182 --> 00:03:27.460
price leaves the band and does not come

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.693
back. On 23 October 2023 the close

00:03:30.693 --> 00:03:34.344
finished above the top line. The price did

00:03:34.344 --> 00:03:36.233
not come back, so this example was

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.269
finished. Write your stop rule down before

00:03:39.269 --> 00:03:41.964
you start. On the card it says: Stop =

00:03:41.964 --> 00:03:47.109
when you quit. Worked check for 19 July

00:03:47.109 --> 00:03:51.627
2023 to 16 October 2023. Six equal gaps of

00:03:51.627 --> 00:03:54.380
about 900 dollars sit between the bottom

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.774
line and the top line. The stop rule is:

00:03:57.774 --> 00:04:00.301
if the daily close leaves the top line and

00:04:00.301 --> 00:04:02.679
does not come back, the idea is finished.

00:04:03.199 --> 00:04:06.333
Nothing in that list is an order. Price

00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:08.853
often moves sideways, bouncing between the

00:04:08.853 --> 00:04:11.685
same top and bottom instead of leaving. A

00:04:11.685 --> 00:04:14.120
grid is a ladder of limit orders built for

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.339
that bouncing, and it has nothing to do

00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:18.702
while price runs one way and stays there.

00:04:19.902 --> 00:04:22.161
A grid has three parts you can name: the

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.004
range, the levels, and the stop. The range

00:04:25.004 --> 00:04:27.459
is the band. The levels are the rungs

00:04:27.459 --> 00:04:30.986
inside it. Buy orders sit on lines below

00:04:30.986 --> 00:04:33.325
the price and sell orders sit on lines

00:04:33.325 --> 00:04:36.195
above it. The sells need some coin, so a

00:04:36.195 --> 00:04:38.809
grid starts with part cash and part coin,

00:04:38.809 --> 00:04:42.511
and that is a description, not advice. No

00:04:42.511 --> 00:04:45.422
order is sent from this lesson. You draw

00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:47.938
the idea. If a screen appears later, it

00:04:47.938 --> 00:04:50.356
should be a copy of the page, and only on

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:53.602
paper or demo. The course is a map, and

00:04:53.602 --> 00:04:55.583
this introduction is only the first

00:04:55.583 --> 00:04:58.327
square. Next is a checklist, then the

00:04:58.327 --> 00:05:01.109
definition, then calm or trending markets,

00:05:01.109 --> 00:05:03.573
then spacing and range, then entry and

00:05:03.573 --> 00:05:05.480
exit, then a paper screen, then

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.103
monitoring, then mistakes, then scaling,

00:05:08.103 --> 00:05:11.895
then an opt-in lesson on liquidation. Draw

00:05:11.895 --> 00:05:14.230
a path that leaves the top of the band and

00:05:14.188 --> 00:05:16.922
does not return. As price climbs, each

00:05:16.922 --> 00:05:19.310
sell order fills, so you end up holding

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.976
cash. As price falls, each buy order

00:05:21.976 --> 00:05:25.456
fills, so you end up holding coin. There

00:05:25.456 --> 00:05:27.655
is no result number in this lesson. A

00:05:27.655 --> 00:05:29.822
result number would pretend the example

00:05:29.716 --> 00:05:33.403
already happened. The example is a drawing

00:05:33.403 --> 00:05:36.300
of a mechanism. The next step is the setup

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.538
checklist, on paper, before any screen.

00:05:39.058 --> 00:05:41.582
You will need the three words when that

00:05:41.582 --> 00:05:44.236
checklist asks what a grid is. A paper or

00:05:44.236 --> 00:05:46.888
demo account is a fence around practice.

00:05:47.408 --> 00:05:49.575
Inside the fence you can see fields and

00:05:49.442 --> 00:05:51.929
buttons. You still do not send an order in

00:05:51.929 --> 00:05:55.293
this course. If you keep one sentence,

00:05:55.293 --> 00:05:57.740
keep this: range, levels, and stop, drawn

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.865
before any click. Bouncing inside the band

00:06:00.865 --> 00:06:03.641
is what a grid is built for. The exit from

00:06:03.641 --> 00:06:06.988
the band is the failure picture. A grid

00:06:06.988 --> 00:06:09.363
bot places waiting buys below the price

00:06:09.363 --> 00:06:13.210
and waiting sells above it. This 2023 path

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.312
stayed between the bottom line and the top

00:06:16.312 --> 00:06:19.148
line, with six gaps of about 900 between

00:06:19.148 --> 00:06:22.465
the lines. The stop rule says what you

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:24.689
will do if the price leaves and does not

00:06:24.512 --> 00:06:27.921
come back. Next lesson: What you are going

00:06:27.921 --> 00:06:30.616
to need. The pair is the two things you

00:06:30.616 --> 00:06:33.461
swap, like Bitcoin and US dollars. Bring

00:06:33.461 --> 00:06:35.517
your notes: the top and bottom of the

00:06:35.408 --> 00:06:37.743
band, the gaps between the lines, and your

00:06:37.624 --> 00:06:40.215
stop rule. Leave every figure marked

00:06:40.215 --> 00:06:42.307
EXAMPLE, and no order is sent between

00:06:42.307 --> 00:06:42.795
lessons.

